{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwHYRAq5HiwzWsHoifDw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0131ukaEXi7PRycnhJWDZK7w","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:50]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"\\\\newcommand{\\\\ln}{\\\\operatorname{ln}}\\n\\n\",\"\")\nrep(\"V2 has the highest final-accuracy rank order reversed relative to the score ordering: the mean final held-out accuracy decreases\",\"The rank order by score is reversed relative to the end-of-training accuracy: the mean final held-out accuracy decreases\")\nrep(\"which shows that the score and the end-of-training accuracy measure different things.\",\"so the score and the end-of-training accuracy measure different things.\")\nrep(\"including the reference trainer, against a limit of $43{,}200$\\\\,s.\",\"including the reference trainer.\")\nrep(\"the single-seed reference slope ($-0.368$) is in the direction of this reading, but it is one seed.\",\"the single-seed reference slope ($-0.368$) is more negative than the point estimate, but it is one seed without an interval and does not by itself support this reading.\")\nrep(\"use more seeds than clusters needed for a smooth bootstrap, and treat\",\"use enough seeds that the cluster bootstrap has a rich resampling support, and treat\")\nrep(\"\\\\citet{Nanda2023ProgressMF} reverse-engineer one-layer transformers trained on modular addition\",\"\\\\citet{Nanda2023ProgressMF} analyze small transformers trained on modular addition mechanistically\")\nrep(\"memorization has been studied empirically during language-model training \\\\citep{Tirumala2022MemorizationWO} and its information content estimated per model \\\\citep{Morris2025HowMD}.\",\"memorization of training data has been studied empirically during language-model training \\\\citep{Tirumala2022MemorizationWO}, and a metho