{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwHt55edgT7ePYmvYcsE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HYZ9LdVaSSx5yZhMSAAMug","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; sed -i 's/label=\"frozen model, 4 seeds: slope and 95% CI\"/label=\"evaluated model, 4 seeds: slope and 95% CI\"/' scripts/build_figures.py; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\ndef rep(a,b,cnt=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)>=1, a[:60]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"the interval covers about half of the slopes that the delay floor and cap permit.\",\"the interval covers about two-fifths of the slopes that the delay floor and cap permit.\")\nrep(\"the interval covers about half of the slopes that the delay floor and cap allow,\",\"the interval covers about two-fifths of the slopes that the delay floor and cap allow,\")\nrep(\"Dotted lines mark the largest slope magnitude attainable with delays confined to $[250, 10{,}000]$ over four width doublings.\",\"Dotted lines mark the largest slope magnitude attainable ($1.107$) when every width-wise mean delay is confined to $[250, 10{,}000]$.\")\nold_start=s.index(\"\\\\emph{Bounded dynamic range.}\")\nold_end=s.index(\"\\\\emph{Distance to a supported verdict.}\")\nnew=r\"\"\"\\emph{Bounded dynamic range.} In this balanced design the slope is a fixed linear contrast of the width-wise mean log-delays $m_d=\\tfrac14\\sum_s\\ln\\Delta_{d,s}$:\n\\begin{equation}\n\\beta=\\sum_{d} w_d\\,m_d,\\qquad (w_{16},\\dots,w_{256})=(-0.2,\\,-0.1,\\,0,\\,0.1,\\,0.2),\n\\end{equation}\nthat is, $\\beta=0.2\\,(m_{256}-m_{16})+0.1\\,(m_{128}-m_{32})$; the middle width carries no weight, and the verdict depends only on how the two widest models compare with the two narrowest. Because every $m_d\\in[\\ln 250,\\ln 10{,}000]$, $|\\beta|\\le 0.3\\ln 40=1.107$, attained by a step profile; a delay falling log-linearly from the cap at $d=16$ to the floor at $d=256$ would give $0.922$. The interval has width $0.939$ and covers $42\\%$ of the attainable range $[-1.107,1.107]$. Its lower arm extends $0.565$ below the point estimate and its upper arm $0.374$ above.\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:old_start]+new+s[old_end:]\nrep(\"Largest attainable $|\\\\text{slope}|$ & $0.922$ \\\\\\\\\",\"Largest attainable $|\\\\text{slope}|$ (step profile) & $1.107$ \\\\\\\\\\nSlope of a log-linear cap-to-floor profile & $0.922$ \\\\\\\\\")\nrep(\"Interval width as fraction of $[-0.922, 0.922]$ & $0.51$ \\\\\\\\\",\"Interval width as fraction of $[-1.107, 1.107]$ & $0.42$ \\\\\\\\\")\n# model equation\nrep(\"The parameter count is $12d^2+(2p+9)d$,\",\"\"\"Writing $z_i=E[x_i]+P_i$ for the embedded tokens $x_1,x_2,x_3{=}$``$=$'', the evaluated model computes\n\\\\begin{equation}\nh=z_3+W_O\\\\,\\\\mathrm{Attn}(z_1,z_2,z_3),\\\\qquad h'=h+W_2\\\\,\\\\mathrm{ReLU}(W_1h+b_1)+b_2,\\\\qquad \\\\text{logits}=m_d\\\\,W_U\\\\,h',\n\\\\end{equation}\nwith $W_\\\\ast=m_dV_\\\\ast$ for the attention and MLP matrices (Modification 3 below; $m_d=1$ recovers the plain parametrization) and $W_U$ the unembedding. The parameter count is $12d^2+(2p+9)d$,\"\"\")\n# readings table + claims ledger in discussion\nrep(\"\\\\paragraph{What would resolve it.}\",\"\"\"\\\\begin{table}[t]\n\\\\centering\n\\\\caption{What each reading of the interval would imply for quantities that are not retained in the artifacts. None of these can be checked with the available records.}\n\\\\label{tab:readings}\n\\\\small\n\\\\begin{tabular}{p{0.22\\\\textwidth}p{0.36\\\\textwidth}p{0.30\\\\textwidth}}\n\\\\toprule\nReading & Implication for per-width delays & Implication for censoring \\\\\\\\\n\\\\midrule\n(a) Little or no width dependence & Similar delays across widths, within seed noise & Censored runs not concentrated at either end \\\\\\\\\n(b) Negative dependence masked by cap and noise & Longer delays at narrow widths, partly hidden at the cap & Censored runs concentrated at narrow widths \\\\\\\\\n(c) Compensation by multipliers & Matched stock-model runs show a steeper slope than evaluated-model runs on the same seeds & Differs between the two models at the same widths \\\\\\\\\n(d) Non-monotone in $\\\\ln d$ & Extremal delay at an intermediate width; contrast $\\\\beta$ near zero & Censoring at both ends or in the middle \\\\\\\\\n\\\\bottomrule\n\\\\end{tabular}\n\\\\end{table}\n\n\\\\paragraph{What would resolve it.}\"\"\")\nrep(\"\\\\paragraph{Limitations.} The evidence concerns\",\"\"\"\\\\begin{table}[t]\n\\\\centering\n\\\\caption{Claims and their status under this study's evidence.}\n\\\\label{tab:claims}\n\\\\small\n\\\\begin{tabular}{p{0.46\\\\textwidth}p{0.17\\\\textwidth}p{0.25\\\\textwidth}}\n\\\\toprule\nClaim & Status & Basis \\\\\\\\\n\\\\midrule\nDelay decreases with width in this setting & Not established & Interval $[-0.585,0.354]$ contains $0$ \\\\\\\\\nDelay is independent of width in this setting & Not established & Same interval also contains slopes down to $-0.585$ \\\\\\\\\nThe measurement was valid & Supported & Completed evaluation, controls $0.012$ vs.\\\\ ceiling $0.10$, no missing episodes \\\\\\\\\nA substantial share of runs is censored & Supported & $8$ of $20$ runs \\\\\\\\\nThe multipliers weaken or remove a width dependence & Not tested & Reference slope has one seed, no interval, no matched ablation \\\\\\\\\nFitting time and generalization time scale differently with width & Not testable & Not retained in the artifacts \\\\\\\\\nFindings carry over to other moduli, fractions, operations & Not tested & One configuration only \\\\\\\\\n\\\\bottomrule\n\\\\end{tabular}\n\\\\end{table}\n\n\\\\paragraph{Limitations.} The evidence concerns\"\"\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(s)\nE\nPYTHONPATH=/agent-tmp/pylib python3 scripts/build_figures.py; for i in 1 2 3; do pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/dev/null 2>&1; done; bibtex paper >/dev/null 2>&1; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/dev/null 2>&1;  pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex 2>&1 | grep -E \"^!|Output written|Undefined|multiply\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1727,"cache_read_input_tokens":189116,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1727},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2dd35f6f-91b7-4850-b942-7d959e7db0b3","uuid":"8a1d6fdd-8beb-4557-be33-b890d747a795","timestamp":"2026-11-11T14:23:40.664Z","request_id":"req_011CgwHt3j3LPb4REUB3NU2P"}
