range $[-1.107,1.107]$. Its lower arm extends $0.565$ below the point estimate and its upper arm $0.374$ above.\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:old_start]+new+s[old_end:]\nrep(\"Largest attainable $|\\\\text{slope}|$ & $0.922$ \\\\\\\\\",\"Largest attainable $|\\\\text{slope}|$ (step profile) & $1.107$ \\\\\\\\\\nSlope of a log-linear cap-to-floor profile & $0.922$ \\\\\\\\\")\nrep(\"Interval width as fraction of $[-0.922, 0.922]$ & $0.51$ \\\\\\\\\",\"Interval width as fraction of $[-1.107, 1.107]$ & $0.42$ \\\\\\\\\")\n# model equation\nrep(\"The parameter count is $12d^2+(2p+9)d$,\",\"\"\"Writing $z_i=E[x_i]+P_i$ for the embedded tokens $x_1,x_2,x_3{=}$``$=$'', the evaluated model computes\n\\\\begin{equation}\nh=z_3+W_O\\\\,\\\\mathrm{Attn}(z_1,z_2,z_3),\\\\qquad h'=h+W_2\\\\,\\\\mathrm{ReLU}(W_1h+b_1)+b_2,\\\\qquad \\\\text{logits}=m_d\\\\,W_U\\\\,h',\n\\\\end{equation}\nwith $W_\\\\ast=m_dV_\\\\ast$ for the attention and MLP matrices (Modification 3 below; $m_d=1$ recovers the plain parametrization) and $W_U$ the unembedding. The parameter count is $12d^2+(2p+9)d$,\"\"\")\n# readings table + claims ledger in discussion\nrep(\"\\\\paragraph{What would resolve it.}\",\"\"\"\\\\begin{table}[t]\n\\\\centering\n\\\\caption{What each reading of the interval would imply for quantities that are not retained in the artifacts. None of these can be checked with the available records.}\n\\\\label{tab:readings}\n\\\\small\n\\\\begin{tabular}{p{0.22\\\\textwidth}p{0.36\\\\textwidth}p{0.30\\\\textwidth}}\n\\\\toprule\nReading & Implication for per-width delays & Implication for censoring \\\\\\\\\n\\\\midrule\n(a) Little or no width dependence & Similar delays across widths, within seed noise & Censored runs not concentrated at either end \\\\\\\\\n(b) Negative dependence masked by cap and noise & Longer delays at narrow widths, partly hidden at the cap & Censored runs concentrated at narrow widths \\\\\\\\\n(c) Compensation by multipliers & Matched stock-model runs show a steeper slope than evaluated-model runs on the same seeds & Differs between the two models at the same widths \\\\\\\\\n(d) Non-monotone in $\\\\ln d$ & Extremal delay at an intermediate width; contrast $\\\\beta$ near zero & Censoring at both ends or in the middle \\\\\\\\\n\\\\bottomrule\n\\\\end{tabular}\n\\\\end{table}\n\n\\\\paragraph{What would resolve it.}\"\"\")\nrep(\"\\\\paragraph{Limitations.} The evidence concerns\",\"\"\"\\\\begin{table}[t]\n\\\\centering\n\\\\caption{Claims and their status under this study's evidence.}\n\\\\label{tab:claims}\n\\\\small\n\\\\begin{tabular}{p{0.46\\\\textwidth}p{0.17\\\\textwidth}p{0.25\\\\textwidth}}\n\\\\toprule\nClaim & Status & Basis \\\\\\\\\n\\\\midrule\nDelay decreases with width in this setting & Not established & Interval $[-0.585,0.354]$ contains $0$ \\\\\\\\\nDelay is independent of width in this setting & Not established & Same interval also contains slopes down to $-0.585$ \\\\\\\\\nThe measurement was valid & Supported & Completed evaluation, controls $0.012$ vs.\\\\ ceiling $0.10$, no missing episodes \\\\\\\\\nA substantial share of runs is censored & Supported & $8$ of $20$ runs \\\\\\\\\nThe multipliers weaken or remove a width dependence & Not tested & Reference slope has one seed, no interval, no matched ablation \\\\\\\\\nFitting time and generalization time scale differently with width & Not testable & Not retained in the artifacts \\\\\\\\\nFindings carry over to other moduli, fractions, operations & Not tested & One configuration only \\\\\\\\\n\\\\bottomrule\n\\\\end{tabular}\n\\\\end{table}\n\n\\\\paragraph{Limitations.} The evidence concerns\"\"\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(s)\nE\nPYTHONPATH=/agent-tmp/pylib python3 scripts/build_figures.py; for i in 1 2 3; do pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/dev/null 2>&1; done; bibtex paper >/dev/null 2>&1; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/dev/null 2>&1;  pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex 2>&1 | grep -E \"^!|Output written|Undefined|mul