{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwHvPy1SCseTn4q9Kmd2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":941,"cache_read_input_tokens":194221,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":941},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2dd35f6f-91b7-4850-b942-7d959e7db0b3","uuid":"60ddca6a-b555-4d90-941b-6d37a2b7c535","timestamp":"2026-11-11T14:24:02.753Z","request_id":"req_011CgwHvNCbSjrdaqGVpLFm6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwHvPy1SCseTn4q9Kmd2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EQMzg6mtLJjD3qZjBqeUt5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\na=\"\\\\subsection{Evaluated model}\"\nnew=r\"\"\"\\paragraph{What the interval does and does not capture.} Each seed fixes both the train/held-out split and the weight initialization, and the design has exactly one run per seed and width. Resampling seeds therefore propagates split and initialization variability jointly, and a seed is the unit of replication; run-to-run nondeterminism within a seed is not separated from it, and cannot be, since no seed is repeated at a width in the sealed design. Because the design is balanced, the pooled OLS slope equals the slope fitted to the width-wise means of $\\ln\\Delta$, and the bootstrap interval is the percentile range of that quantity over seed resamples.\n\n\"\"\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,new+a,1)\nb=\"\\\\paragraph{Alternative readings that the data cannot separate.}\"\nnew2=r\"\"\"\\paragraph{Relation to the explanations of grokking.} Each account in Section~\\ref{sec:related} associates the delay with a quantity that can depend on width or parametrization: memorization capacity (how early the training split is fitted), initial weight norm and the loss landscape, the relative efficiency of memorizing and generalizing circuits, and the position on the lazy-to-rich axis. The evaluated model touches the last two knobs directly: its initial weights are shrunk by half, which the source comments describe as aimed at reducing lazy-regime memorization, and its multipliers change how large a step each layer takes at a given width. A clear width slope from this model could therefore reflect the multipliers rather than width alone, and a flat slope could reflect their compensating a stock-model dependence. This is why the isolating comparison with a matched stock model (Section~\\ref{sec:discussion}, item iv) matters more than a further estimate of the slope for the evaluated model alone.\n\n\"\"\"\nassert b in s\ns=s.replace(b,new2+b,1)\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(s)\nE\nfor i in 1 2; do pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/dev/null 2>&1; done; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex 2>&1 | grep -E \"^!|Output written\"; PYTHONPATH=/agent-tmp/pylib python3 /agent-tmp/pagefill.py 2>/dev/null"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":941,"cache_read_input_tokens":194221,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":941},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2dd35f6f-91b7-4850-b942-7d959e7db0b3","uuid":"935799ac-dcc2-47f5-af11-5de8213d2def","timestamp":"2026-11-11T14:24:08.752Z","request_id":"req_011CgwHvNCbSjrdaqGVpLFm6"}
