ence.episodes\",M+\"combined_score\"])\nadd(\"Derived: fitted multiplicative delay factor per width doubling is 0.980 (interval 0.557 to 1.425); over 16->256 it is 0.924 (interval 0.096 to 4.12); at the reference slope 0.230.\",[M+\"grok_delay_log_slope\",M+\"grok_delay_slope_ci_low\",M+\"grok_delay_slope_ci_high\",M+\"reference_delay_log_slope\"])\nadd(\"Derived: with delay floored at 250 and capped at 10,000 steps (ratio 40), OLS weights (-0.2,-0.1,0,0.1,0.2) over widths 16..256 give a maximum attainable |slope| of 0.3*ln(40)=1.107; a log-linear cap-to-floor profile gives 0.922.\",[\"final.evidence.episodes\"])\nadd(\"Derived: interval width 0.939, covering 42% of [-1.107,1.107]; arms 0.565 below and 0.374 above the point estimate.\",[M+\"grok_delay_log_slope\",M+\"grok_delay_slope_ci_low\",M+\"grok_delay_slope_ci_high\"])\nadd(\"Derived: a point estimate below -0.374 would have been needed for a 'supported' verdict with the same upper arm; the reference slope plus the same upper arm gives +0.006 (illustrative arithmetic).\",[M+\"grok_delay_log_slope\",M+\"grok_delay_slope_ci_high\",M+\"reference_delay_log_slope\"])\nadd(\"Derived: with four seeds there are C(7,4)=35 distinct seed multisets; 4/4^4=1/64 of draws are one seed repeated four times.\",[\"final.evidence.episodes\"])\nadd(\"Workload: modular addition modulo 97, 3,763 training and 5,646 held-out pairs, widths 16-256, 10,000 steps probed every 250, AdamW lr 1e-3, betas (0.9,0.98), weight decay 1.0, 2,000 bootstrap resamples, fit/generalization threshold 0.99 (evaluator workload manifest in source_evidence/workload/final_manifest.json and evaluator source).\",[\"final.evidence.episodes\",\"final.qualification.status\"])\nadd(\"Parameter count 12d^2+(2p+9)d: 6,320 at d=16 to 838,400 at d=256; multipliers (128/d)^0.5 = 2.83, 2.0, 1.41, 1.0, 0.71 (from source_evidence/frozen_model/program.py).\",[\"final.qualification.status\"])\nadd(\"Compute: 1,804 RPC calls (limit 2,200) over 22 episodes and 11,764 s elapsed in the final evaluation (source_evidence/final/final_manifest.json).\",[\"final.qualification.status\",\"final.evidence.episodes\"])\nadd(\"Development-plane configurations (modulus 53, fraction 0.5, widths 32/64/128, 2 seeds) scored 0.798, 0.828, 0.850 with 4/6, 6/6, 4/6 runs censored; mean final held-out accuracy 0.981, 0.944, 0.921; per-seed scores of the third span the other two means.\",[\"result.improvement_001\",\"result.improvement_002\",\"result.improvement_003\"])\nadd(\"Development-plane control maximum held-out accuracy about 0.023, 0.022, 0.023 for the three configurations.\",[\"result.improvement_001\",\"result.improvement_002\",\"result.improvement_003\"])\nadd(\"Grokking background: Power et al. report delayed generalization on small algorithmic datasets including modular arithmetic.\",[\"ref.s2.a1d1983a7b19845141e6505bd32dc395e5a136ba\"],[\"Power2022GrokkingGB\"])\nadd(\"Nanda et al. analyze small transformers on modular addition mechanistically and define progress measures.\",[\"ref.s2.f680d47a51a0e470fcb228bf0110c026535ead1b\"],[\"Nanda2023ProgressMF\"])\nadd(\"Omnigrok analyzes loss landscape and weight norm beyond algorithmic data.\",[\"ref.s2.ad065eed8e1f727a8b0d8675802e4ffb1fcb87b4\"],[\"Liu2022OmnigrokGB\"])\nadd(\"Kumar et al. relate grokking to a lazy-to-rich transition, analyzed in two-layer regression.\",[\"ref.s2.287839feb1e302fe513c2b03754ca44ad428634a\"],[\"Kumar2023GrokkingAT\"])\nadd(\"Huang et al. discuss grokking, double descent and emergent abilities via circuits competition.\",[\"ref.s2.7d417465bdf254f8b4491c0e4adbace8f49010ab\"],[\"Huang2024UnifiedVO\"])\nadd(\"Varma et al. explain grokking through circuit efficiency.\",[\"ref.task.Varma2023ExplainingGT\"],[\"Varma2023ExplainingGT\"])\nadd(\"Davies et al. unify grokking and double descent.\",[\"ref.task.Davies2023UnifyingGA\"],[\"Davies2023UnifyingGA\"])\nadd(\"Double descent with model size (Nakkiran), fitting random labels (Zhang), memorization dynamics (Tirumala), information estimate per data point (Morris).\",[\"ref.task.Nakkiran2019DeepDD\",\"ref.task.Zhang2016UnderstandingDL\",\"ref.task.Tirumala2022MemorizationWO\",\"ref.task.Morris2025HowMD\"],[\"Nakkiran2019DeepDD\",\"Zhang2016UnderstandingDL\",\"Tirumala2022MemorizationWO\",\"Morris2025HowMD\"])\nadd(\"Effective learning rates under normalization (Lyle), practical measures of dynamical richness (Nam), decoupled weight decay (Loshchilov).\",[\"ref.s2.e7c70877bc10d7d430f67489da78b227ac08a17a\",\"ref.s2.d6f9d7b5ddba8192670cb0ecb3d75108aa610d6f\",\"ref.task.Loshchilov2017DecoupledWD\"],[\"Lyle2024NormalizationAE\",\"Nam2024DecouplingDR\",\"Loshchilov2017DecoupledWD\"])\njson.dump({\"claims\":C},open('claims_grounding.json','w'),indent=1)\nprint(len(C))\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1347,"cache_read_input_tokens":204115,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1347},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2dd35f6f-91b7-4850-b942-7d959e7db0b3","uuid":"5f270d94-2950-4941-971a-f20797e2bbe7","timestamp":"2026-11-11T14:24:58.892Z","request_id":"req_011CgwHyboVgpmYstcHsAA4d"}
